How this update is applied. `store` opens the platform marketplace;
`direct` downloads and self-installs. `lx.supports('app.selfUpdate')`
is true only for `direct`.

types.description:
Host app identity. Everything here is fixed for the life of the process;
the language the app renders in is not, and lives on
`lx.host.displayLanguage`.

What an `lx` call rejects with. Branch on `code`, never on `message`:

```ts
async function pickFolder() {
  try {
    return await lx.pick.directory()
  } catch (e) {
    if (isLxError(e) && e.code === 'E_NOT_SUPPORTED') return null
    throw e
  }
}
```

